<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
		<PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
		<Title>TestFramework.Core</Title>
		<Authors>DeadMoon0</Authors>
		<Product>TestFramework</Product>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<PackageTags>Test;UnitTest;IntegrationTest;Framework;Fluent;Timeline</PackageTags>
		<PackageIcon>Icon.png</PackageIcon>
		<Description>The core package of the TestFramework ecosystem for building integration-style and end-to-end test workflows. Provides the timeline engine for steps, events, variables, artifacts, retries, timeouts, and assertions, and serves as the foundation for extension packages like Azure, LocalIO, and Simple.</Description>
		<Version>0.7.0</Version>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/DeadMoon0/TestFramework-Core</PackageProjectUrl>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/DeadMoon0/TestFramework-Core.git</RepositoryUrl>
		<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
		<Copyright>Copyright (c) DeadMoon0 2026</Copyright>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>BREAKING - renamed for one spelling per concept: WithTimeOut is WithTimeout, the step modifier Name(...) is Label(...), Transform takes the source variable first, Transform(from, to, fn), and SetVariable takes a plain value while SetVariableFrom copies another variable; a variable passed to SetVariable is refused when the timeline is built. BREAKING - SetupRun takes output.WriteLine instead of xunit's ITestOutputHelper, and no public member takes optional parameters any more: exceptions, IO declarations, polling results, debugger signals and the graph records use overloads and init properties. BREAKING - step labels are case-sensitive like every other name, and the plan check no longer passes a variable read with a different case. BREAKING - every exception Core throws now derives from TimelineFrameworkException: failed assertions from AssertionFailedException (printed as ASSERTION FAILED, with the line that made them) and TimelineRunFailedException printed as RUN FAILED. Text, order and count assertions are extensions constrained to strings, IComparable&lt;T&gt; and IEnumerable, so a misuse no longer compiles. An assertion on a variable never set fails, EnsureRanToCompletion fails for a step that never ran, and the blocking PersistentEnvironmentContext constructors are gone; use CreateAsync. The builder interfaces can be used but no longer implemented outside Core, so later verbs break nobody. New: RunServices.Owned, RunRecord&lt;T&gt;, ArtifactStore.Assign, VariableStore.SetSecretVariable, EnvComponent.StateOf, and a fresh environment per run through IRunScopedEnvironmentFactory, read back from TimelineRun.Environment.</PackageReleaseNotes>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
	  <None Include="..\Modules\TestFramework-Common\Assets\Icon.png">
	    <Pack>True</Pack>
	    <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
	  </None>
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<!-- Core's own suite, and nobody else. A grant to another package's suite is the same private
		     handshake as a grant to the package: whatever that suite may reach for, every other package's
		     suite may not - and it hides that a surface is missing. Config's suite never used one, and
		     Simple's hand-built the run's pieces until RunContext.Detached existed to hand them over. -->
		<AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Runtime.CompilerServices.InternalsVisibleTo">
			<_Parameter1>TestFramework.Core.Tests</_Parameter1>
		</AssemblyAttribute>
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="Newtonsoft.Json" Version="13.0.4" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
	  <None Include="README.md">
	    <Pack>True</Pack>
	    <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
	  </None>
	</ItemGroup>

</Project>
